### Appendix B: Derivation of the Generalized Averaging Model

This appendix provides the step‑by‑step derivation of the first‑harmonic GAM for the N‑phase DAB under TPS modulation, following Uicich et al. (2021). Only the key equations are reproduced; the full development is available in the cited reference.

**B.1 Fourier Series Representation**
For a state variable \( x(\tau) \), the time‑varying Fourier coefficient is
\[ \langle x \rangle_k (t) = \frac{1}{T_s} \int_{t-T_s}^t x(\tau) e^{-j k \omega_s \tau} d\tau. \]

**B.2 Inductor Current Dynamics**
Under TPS, the transformer current in module \( m \) is piecewise linear. Its first‑harmonic phasor \( \bar{i}_{L,m} \) obeys
\[ L_m \frac{d}{dt} \begin{pmatrix} \Re\{\bar{i}_{L,m}\} \\ \Im\{\bar{i}_{L,m}\} \end{pmatrix} = \frac{2\sqrt{2}}{\pi} \begin{pmatrix} v_{\text{in}} \sin\phi_m - \frac{v_o}{n_m} \sin(\phi_m - \delta_m) \\ -v_{\text{in}} \cos\phi_m + \frac{v_o}{n_m} \cos(\phi_m - \delta_m) \end{pmatrix} - \omega_s L_m \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -1 \\ 1 & 0 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} \Re\{\bar{i}_{L,m}\} \\ \Im\{\bar{i}_{L,m}\} \end{pmatrix}, \]
where \( \phi_m, \delta_m \) are the outer and inner phase shifts.

**B.3 Output Capacitor Dynamics**
The DC‑side dynamics are obtained by averaging the rectified current:
\[ C_{\text{out}} \dot{v}_o = \sum_{m=1}^k \frac{2}{\pi} |\bar{i}_{L,m}| \cos(\arg(\bar{i}_{L,m})) - \frac{P}{v_o}. \]

These equations constitute the full GAM used in Chapter 2.

