### Appendix F: Experimental Validation Protocol

This appendix restates the falsifiable hypotheses and test procedures from §7.5 in a structured format suitable for a laboratory workbook.

**F.1 Hypothesis H₁ – CPL Stability Test**
- **Equipment:** 6‑phase DAB prototype, electronic load (CPL mode), 12‑bit oscilloscope.
- **Procedure:** Set \( v_{\text{ref}} = 800\,\text{V} \), initial load 30 kW. Step load to 60 kW at 10 MW/s. Record \( v_o(t) \).
- **Pass criterion:** \( |v_o(t)-v_{\text{ref}}| \le 8\,\text{V} \) for \( t \ge 50\,\text{ms} \); steady‑state ripple \( \le 2\,\text{V}_{\text{pp}} \).

**F.2 Hypothesis H₂ – Thermal Safety Test**
- **Conditions:** \( T_{\text{amb}} = 50^\circ\text{C} \).
- **Procedure:** Ramp load to 350 kW in 30 s, hold 15 min. Measure \( T_j \) of hottest MOSFET with IR camera.
- **Pass criterion:** \( \max T_j \le 125^\circ\text{C} \).

**F.3 Hypothesis H₃ – Efficiency Test**
- **Procedure:** Measure efficiency at 30 %, 50 %, 70 %, 100 % load with all phases active and with phase‑shedding active.
- **Pass criterion:** Efficiency at 30 % load with shedding ≥ 2 % higher than all‑phases baseline; at 100 % load, degradation ≤ 0.5 %.

**F.4 Hypothesis H₄ – Uncertainty Quantification Test**
- **Procedure:** Characterise 30 production devices, run 10 000 Monte Carlo simulations using measured distributions.
- **Pass criterion:** Upper 95 % confidence bound on violation probability \( \le 10^{-3} \).

